# LeakSanitizer suppressions for third-party libraries (one reason per line).

# minizip-ng (openssl backend, Linux): reading a deliberately corrupted ZIP leaks the 24-byte
# hash state that the library itself creates on its error path. Not ours: our own hash use
# (io/src/fission_file.cpp) creates and deletes its state in one function.
leak:mz_crypt_sha_create
